.planning/impact-map/COVERAGE-ROADMAP.md:5:This roadmap controls the progressive whole-repo impact-map program. It keeps OpenClaw coverage broad enough that every future file change can be placed somewhere, while preventing shallow notes from being mistaken for verified impact knowledge.
.planning/impact-map/COVERAGE-ROADMAP.md:7:For the operational file-change workflow, use [`CHANGE-IMPACT-WORKFLOW.md`](CHANGE-IMPACT-WORKFLOW.md); this roadmap owns promotion/demotion, wave gates, and graph/tool freshness policy. For the verified-wave execution order, use [`../VERIFIED-WAVE-RUNBOOK.md`](../VERIFIED-WAVE-RUNBOOK.md).
.planning/impact-map/COVERAGE-ROADMAP.md:31:### `deep-partial` → `verified`
.planning/impact-map/COVERAGE-ROADMAP.md:33:A module can move to `verified` only when it has:
.planning/impact-map/COVERAGE-ROADMAP.md:40:Graph output alone cannot promote a module to `verified`; the slice boundary, freshness, and validation evidence must be recorded together.
.planning/impact-map/COVERAGE-ROADMAP.md:44:If code changes or tool coverage becomes stale, demote `verified` to `deep-partial` or `partial` according to the remaining evidence. If leaf-level file-role/code-path evidence is stale or untrusted, demote to `partial` until fresh evidence is recorded.
